 It has been brought to my attention that my patches to Scrabble to
allow it to run under MS-DOS were basically worthless.  To get the
diffs, I just ran "diff oldfile.c newfile.c" and piped the output
to files.  The diff program was the diff program supplied with
PiCnix, a collection of Unix utilities for DOS.  However, patch will
not handle the resulting diffs.  So, I moved everything over to Unix,
and used "diff -c" on the files, and combined all the patches into
one nice file.  Here is a new Shar file to replace the one I previously
posted:


